The libraries already draw progress bars on a terminal (Hugging Face's tqdm hides them when output is not a terminal, and a pseudo-terminal with a 0x0 window size draws them 0 columns wide, which first made it look as if there were none). So the bars are left to the libraries, and only a line naming the model is added, printed when the model is not in the local cache. The cache is checked with local_files_only lookups, not a call to the Hub, so a cached run makes no extra network request. The sizes are in the README, not in the messages: the bars show them, and sizes in code would go stale. DISABLE_SAFETENSORS_CONVERSION is set because transformers' auto conversion downloads a converted model.safetensors from a PR revision of the aligner repo in a non-daemon thread, so the process stayed alive about 100 s after Done; later runs load pytorch_model.bin from main and never use that copy. Considered pre-downloading the Whisper model with snapshot_download for a bar of our own; not needed once the bars turned out to show.
